<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE - SNP 1997 PLUNGES INTO RED.</title>
<headline>TABLE - SNP 1997 PLUNGES INTO RED.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 1.83  vs  0.08 (gain)</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	   (loss) 3.22  vs  0.14 (gain)</p>
<p>    Turnover				40.81  vs 40.98</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.79  vs  0.83</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   1.51  vs  1.43</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation    4.29  vs  3.38</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			   1.96  vs  0.46 (gain)</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	    0.66  vs  0.40</p>
<p>    Tax					0.56  vs  0.78</p>
<p>    Minorities		    (loss) 0.04  vs  nil</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	     (gain) 0.14  vs  0.04 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Printing and publishing firm SNP Corporation Ltd said it recorded a first half loss because of an erosion of sales and margins in the competitive general printing market.</p>
